          "kicker": "Tournament standings",
          "heading": "Fiji drop to bottom of the table after losing to Scotland",
          "body": "Fiji sit bottom of the table after suffering three consecutive defeats in their current campaign. The team has scored 49 points across those three matches. They have also conceded 145 points during the same period, leaving them with a point difference of minus 96. This run follows a 17-33 loss to Scotland in their last fixture. It contrasts with 2023, when the side reached a peak of No. 7 in the world rankings."
