      "edition": "Wednesday 23 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Winning streak ends",
          "heading": "England Women's rugby team draw with Canada finishing historic unbeaten run",
          "body": "The Red Roses’ remarkable sequence of 39 successive Test victories has come to a close following a 26-26 draw against Canada at Sandy Park. Despite England leading late into the final quarter, they were unable to secure the win after a Canadian ruck turnover denied a potential match-winning score. John Mitchell reflected on the result, stating: “We were applying huge pressure, but we just didn’t convert. One Test match isn’t going to take us away from our purpose.”"
        },
