      "edition": "Wednesday 23 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Test match win",
          "heading": "France Women defeat Australia in dramatic comeback after stadium fire delay",
          "body": "France Women secured a 29-26 victory over Australia in a chaotic Test match in Aix-en-Provence on Saturday. The hosts overcame a 19-point deficit and a mid-match delay caused by a burning bus outside the Stade Maurice David. Despite being reduced to 11 players during a turbulent first half, France rallied with 17 unanswered points in the final 25 minutes to complete the win. Coach Tim Walsh noted the Wallaroos were disappointed to let the match slip after the momentum shift."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Japan men win Pacific Nations Cup after beating Fiji",
