      "date": "2026-09-23",
      "edition": "Wednesday 23 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "WXV campaign",
          "heading": "Ireland Women succumb to USA comeback in WXV Global Series opener",
          "body": "The Ireland Women’s rugby team suffered a frustrating 40-36 defeat against the USA in their WXV Global Series opener. Despite holding a 19-point lead following tries from Vicky Elmes Kinlan, Cliodhna Moloney-MacDonald, Aoife Wafer, and Erin King, the hosts were overhauled in the second half. Head coach Scott Bemand admitted it was \"a game we should have won,\" citing a loss of discipline and technical errors as the primary factors that allowed the USA to gain momentum."
        },
        {
