        {
          "kicker": "Tournament success",
          "heading": "Japan Brave Blossoms claim Pacific Nations Cup title after beating Fiji",
          "body": "Japan’s men secured their first Pacific Nations Cup title since 2019 after a 20-15 victory over Fiji at Prince Chichibu Memorial Stadium. The result, which elevated the team into the world’s top 10 rankings, was driven by a determined defensive effort and a decisive second-half try from Ben Gunter. Captain Naoto Saito hailed the breakthrough, stating, “It’s a great breakthrough to create history for Japan. It gives this young team great confidence. This is going to be the trigger for us.”"
        },
        {
